ox;color:rgb(104,118,135)\"><br></span></span></code></pre></div><div>for <div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">dygraphOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;plot1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Look at the shiny dygraphs demo, it is easy to see how dygraph_date_window is returned to shinyServer, but it is not intuitive to me how I can obtain other information, such nearest data points using &quot;plot_click&quot; or &quot;plot_hover&quot; with dygrpha. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>-Yu</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
